From 1c941b15d32388107c6a9b668c8a24edc90ea45e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Audia <therealgraysky@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:08:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Isolate service logs in a dedicated journal namespace

Run raspisump.service and rsumpweb.service with LogNamespace=raspisump
so their log output lands in its own journal store
(/var/log/journal/<machine-id>.raspisump) instead of the system journal.

get_journal_log() and rsumpsupport now query the unit's LogNamespace=
property and pass --namespace to journalctl only when one is set, so
installs that run the units without a namespace behave exactly as
before.

The new journald@raspisump.conf pins Storage=persistent and caps the
namespace store (64M) to stay SD-card friendly. Debian packaging ships
both new files, adds the acl dependency for setfacl, drops raspisump
from systemd-journal on upgrade, and removes the namespace store on
purge.
